Rulebox: rules for the Cursor agent.

The full rules are in AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md at the repo root. Read both
before doing anything. CLAUDE.md is binding and wins on any disagreement.
The current phase is Phase 3: follow docs/plans/phase-3-staff-shell.md step
by step, and see each step's "Done when" check pass before the next step.

The short list that must never be missed:

1. Never run destructive things on this machine: creating or changing
   Windows accounts, writing Winlogon/policy/LSA values, loading another
   user's registry hive, signing a session out, installing the Rulebox
   service, or running rulebox-agent enroll/recover/unenroll/service
   install for real. Only the user runs those, on the test VM.
2. Never create HKLM\SOFTWARE\Rulebox\TestMachine.
3. Do not edit apps/agent, apps/shell-launcher, crates/rulebox-ipc or
   crates/rulebox-win32 from a Phase 3 step. The IPC contract is frozen.
   If you need a change there, stop and tell the user.
4. The Staff App has no admin rights. Privileged work goes through the
   agent over IPC. Never log or store a password, PIN, hash, device secret
   or enrollment code.
5. Offline-first: bundle fonts, icons and every asset. Icons are Solar only
   (see CLAUDE.md). No CDN, no runtime icon API.
6. Git: commit as the repo's own identity, never change git config, no AI
   attribution of any kind (no Co-Authored-By, no "Generated with"), one
   commit per plan step, and never push or open a PR without the user's
   explicit go-ahead.
7. Use pnpm only. One Cargo workspace and one target/ at the repo root,
   debug builds only. Warn before a step that builds several GB.
8. Develop against the simulated agent:
   cargo run -p rulebox-agent -- run --console --simulate --sim-demo --sim-staff-session
9. Verify for real: clippy and tests for the touched crate, pnpm typecheck
   and pnpm lint, and run the UI and look at it. State plainly what you
   could not verify.
10. If a Done-when check fails twice, or the PRD and the plan disagree,
    stop and ask the user.
